# plans branch only (orphan) — never part of a code PR or upstream.
# The sync-main watcher rewrites this heartbeat file every 60s; it is
# machine-local liveness, not shared project state, so keep it out of git.
session/status/main.md

# Raw per-session capture written continuously by scripts/session-snapshot.sh, plus its
# marker. Regenerable from the session transcript, uncurated, and per-machine — it exists
# so panic recovery is reading a small file rather than parsing a large one. The distilled,
# committed artifact is the digest beside it.
session/digests/*.raw.md
session/digests/.*.mark
session/digests/.*.log

# Handoffs are ephemeral coordination, not permanent artifacts, per CONVENTIONS.md's own
# framing: "need not be committed by the submitting session... the sync session reads
# uncommitted handoff files directly," and .DONE files are meant to be git rm'd, not kept.
# The .md/.WIP/.DONE state transitions happen via bare mv (never git mv), so a broad
# git add/commit that happens to sweep this directory records an unrelated delete+add pair
# rather than a tracked rename -- accidentally tracked, not deliberately. Dean's ruling
# (2026-08-16, plan__handoff-git-tracking-inconsistency-found.md): "These are pointers
# anyway. The sync__ handoff should track the important history" -- the durable record
# belongs in CURRENT.md and each scope's own Type-3 docs, not in a handoff file's git log.
# NOT retroactive: the ~439 handoff files already tracked as of 2026-08-16 stay tracked,
# no history rewrite. This only stops NEW accidental tracking going forward.
session/handoffs/*.md
session/handoffs/*.md.WIP
session/handoffs/*.md.DONE
session/handoffs/*.md.RETRACTED
